    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0509" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg437"/>

                <head>Inhabitants of Canzo</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source"
                    >[Translation.]<lb/>[Extract.]</note>
                <dateline>No. 106 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Congress Street</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn, L. I.</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-20">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 20, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>I have the honor of informing you that the citizens of Canzo, Province of Como,
                    Lombardy, Italy, wishing to express their veneration and sympathy for the great
                    martyr to the cause of emancipation and the Union, our lamented President,
                    Abraham Lincoln, unanimously passed a resolution to call after his name the new
                    square by the side of the national road in their town. They wished their
                    resolution should reach your Excellency’s hands, and intrusted to me the care of
                    fulfilling their desire.</p>
                <p> * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Please receive my highest feelings of regard, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ACHILLE MAGNI</signed>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Andrew Johnson</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">President of the United States of America</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
